# Service registry. Each service has:
#   port      — TCP port (or "stdio" for non-port servers, or "" for none)
#   workdir   — directory to cd into before running the command
#   cmd       — command line to launch the service
#   needs     — space-separated dependencies (problade / network / etc.)
#   note      — short human description
#
# rr-dash is treated specially — status only, no Start/Stop from this wrapper
# (you don't want the dashboard killing itself from inside a request handler).
#
# rag-mcp is also status-only — Claude Desktop / Cowork launches it via its MCP
# config; running it standalone from a shell is rarely useful.

# rag-ui moved 5000 → 5050 on 2026-07-02: macOS AirPlay Receiver squats on 5000.
